"Drathok is bound to the pit lord Elasar by a true soul contract; Elasar owns him."
"Drathok cannot attack Elasar, nor ask anyone else to."
"Elasar holds Drathok's daughter; Drathok has not seen her in over two years and fears her dead."
"Drathok meant to sell Markus to a god, to buy back his daughter and settle his debt to Elasar."
"Drathok came under Elasar so his people would have a safe haven; Lexi calls him an idealist."
"Drathok wants Lexi to lead his people if he dies."
"If Drathok frees Markus himself, Elasar will slaughter every imp and worker bound to Drathok."
"If Drathok dies, his contracts, Markus's among them, pass to Elasar."
"Elasar beat Drathok for not offering Markus as tribute; it left a black eye and melted horn tips."
"On Elasar's order Drathok lied that a god's gift bought Markus out, to cut Markus off from gods."
"Drathok set Markus's double bout hoping he would die before Randall came, then wanted him to win."
"In Randall's bout Drathok silently let Markus near escape through the broken wall."
"Drathok readied a suicidal shot of his relic mana cannon, ready to die so Markus could go free."
"Drathok gave Markus his malichor sabre and his own mana in that fight."
"Drathok struck a deal with Serena: she mends the arena, he tells Elasar Markus came through whole."
"Drathok keeps the lie to Elasar that Markus is still himself and did not break."
"Drathok told Serena his soul is not for sale."
"Drathok finds Firrelia grey."
"Drathok called Mana Manipulation useless to hide its worth, and told gods Earth breeds warriors."
"Drathok knows gods visit Markus, and warned that others can know it too."
"Drathok's relic mana cannon was knocked from Markus's hands in the arena; where it lies is unknown."
"Drathok's contract over Markus is a facsimile, weaker than a true soul contract."
"Serena's quests name Drathok as a kill; she also hints he could replace Elasar over the demons."
"Randall offers to kill Drathok to take Markus's contract, accepting war with Thiron demons."
